# This repo is the cloud fine-tuning environment. It exists BECAUSE the repo it
# was carved out of accumulated 100MB+ corpus blobs and became unpushable
# (V-309). Everything here is aimed at not repeating that.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Machine-local state a cloud session generates at runtime. `ledger/` in
# particular appeared untracked at the repo root during a dry run.
#
# `cloud-sessions/state/` covers the runtime churn: `fleet/` heartbeat files and
# `exodus-manifest.json`. It does NOT un-track the two files already committed
# there (`README.md` and the empty `sessions.jsonl` dispatch ledger) — gitignore
# only ever applies to untracked paths, so AGENT.md's "tracked on purpose since
# 2026-08-14" and this rule are both true at once. Noted 2026-08-24 because the
# two statements read as a contradiction otherwise.
ledger/
cloud-sessions/state/
*.log

# `run.sh` rewrites this on every run. It is a per-run log, not a record: the
# archived copy was removed in the 2026-08-24 trim precisely because its numbers
# were measured against a different repo and invited miscitation. Generate it
# locally; never commit one repo's run log into another's history.
cloud-sessions/tests/RESULTS.md

# Run artifacts. This is the large-blob rule: a run directory may hold a
# multi-hundred-MB corpus, which is exactly what made the parent repo
# unpushable. Only the small synthetic QA fixture is tracked, deliberately.
fine-tuning/factory-product/runs/*
!fine-tuning/factory-product/runs/qa-dryrun-synth/

# Secrets — never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
